Slice 079b (R-T30, R-SO10, Q3 of slice 079, dispute D1 of slice 079), the `roc` on `PATH` as the selected compiler of a tool command (entry `commands`). The home of `tc1-order` (4 installed compilers: A = nightly-2026-10-14-38a3029, B = nightly-2026-10-12-2664a27, C = nightly-2026-10-05-aaaaaaa, D = nightly-2026-10-01-bbbbbbb) but `config.toml` has no `default-roc` (only `[probe] timeout = 20`), and `ROC_TOOLCHAIN` is not set. The `roc` on `PATH` (`fx/path-roc`, `fx/jobs` `version`) has the id C: a nightly that has a toolchain dir, and not the newest. So ranks 2 and 6 give nothing and rank 7 selects C.
The pin of each app is `nightly-2026-10-11-1a2b3c4` (not installed, in the nightly list), a fake tty, `TALON_NOW=2026-10-15T12:00:00Z`. `fx/answers` is empty. The checks are the rows of `fx/units`: `two` fails with A only, `three` fails with A, C and D.

| Run | Words | Result | Rules |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| 1 | `tool install acme/two` | The `path_roc` lookup (the calls of slice 022b: the cache, `roc version`) runs once, when the choice starts, because ranks 2 and 6 give nothing. C is selected, so the round of checks is C, A, B, D (the selected one first, as in `tc1-order`). C passes, so the build runs with C only. `built with C`. No download, no `default-roc` write (a try is no download) | R-T30, R-SO10, R-T17, R-T19 |
| 2 | `tool install acme/three env:ROC_TOOLCHAIN=nightly-2026-10-12-2664a27` | `ROC_TOOLCHAIN` (rank 2) selects B and beats the `PATH` `roc` (rank 7): there is no `path_roc` call in this run. The round of checks is B, A, C, D (the selected one first, as in `tc1-order` run 2): `three` passes with B only, so the build runs with B | R-T30, R-SO2, R-SO7 |
| 3 | `tool install acme/dl --roc pinned` | `--roc pinned` skips the try. The `path_roc` lookup is answered from the cache (`path-roc.json` is read, nothing runs). The pin is downloaded (the flag is the consent). A compiler is selected (the `PATH` one), so the download becomes no default: `config.toml` is read by the download as always, and never written (in `tc2-nothing`, with no selected compiler, it becomes the default) | R-T30, R-SO15, R-SO14, R-T16, R-T6 |

The unpack of the app bundle is not part of this rule: `Fetch.unbundler` (R-FE4) takes the newest installed compiler (A) when no `default-roc` names one.
